    "markdown": "![Hugging Face's logo](https://huggingface.co/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face⟨1⟩\n  *  Models ⟨2⟩\n  *  Datasets ⟨3⟩\n  *  Spaces ⟨4⟩\n  *  Buckets new⟨5⟩\n  *  Docs ⟨6⟩\n  *  Enterprise ⟨7⟩\n  * Pricing⟨8⟩\n  *     * Website\n      *  Tasks⟨9⟩\n      *  HuggingChat⟨10⟩\n      *  Collections⟨11⟩\n      *  Languages⟨12⟩\n      *  Organizations⟨13⟩\n    * Community\n      *  Blog⟨14⟩\n      *  Posts⟨15⟩\n      *  Daily Papers⟨16⟩\n      *  Hardware⟨17⟩\n      *  Learn⟨18⟩\n      *  Discord⟨19⟩\n      *  Forum⟨20⟩\n      *  GitHub⟨21⟩\n    * Solutions\n      *  Team & Enterprise⟨7⟩\n      *  Hugging Face PRO⟨22⟩\n      *  Enterprise Support⟨23⟩\n      *  Inference Providers⟨24⟩\n      *  Inference Endpoints⟨25⟩\n      *  Storage Buckets⟨5⟩\n  * * * *\n  * Log In⟨26⟩\n  * Sign Up⟨27⟩\n\n\n#   Datasets:⟨3⟩\n* * *\n ![](https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/636865b8cca0a0a962c21f3f/n1PEv1RXr_QrhK7DIZbOg.png) ⟨28⟩\nAI4Manufacturing⟨28⟩\n/\nD05-annotated⟨29⟩\nlike 0\nFollow\n![⟨30⟩] AI4Manufacturing 13\nTasks:  Visual Question Answering ⟨31⟩ Image Classification ⟨32⟩\nModalities:  Image ⟨33⟩ Text ⟨34⟩\nFormats:  parquet ⟨35⟩\nLanguages:  English ⟨36⟩\nSize:  10K - 100K ⟨37⟩\nTags:  manufacturing ⟨38⟩ industrial-anomaly-detection ⟨39⟩ defect-detection ⟨40⟩ defect-classification ⟨41⟩ chain-of-thought ⟨42⟩ vision-language ⟨43⟩ + 1\nLibraries:  Datasets ⟨44⟩ Dask ⟨45⟩ Polars ⟨46⟩ + 1\nLicense:\ncc-by-nc-sa-4.0\n Dataset card ⟨29⟩ Data Studio ⟨47⟩ Files Files and versions xet ⟨48⟩ Community ⟨49⟩\n##  You need to agree to share your contact information to access this dataset\nThis repository is publicly accessible, but you have to accept the conditions to access its files and content.\nThis dataset is derived from MMAD and is licensed CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0 (non-commercial). Access requires approval.\nLog in⟨50⟩ or Sign Up⟨51⟩ to review the conditions and access this dataset content.\n  * Schema⟨52⟩\n  * Roles⟨53⟩\n  * How it was built⟨54⟩\n  * 2026-07-18 fix package⟨55⟩\n  * Intended use & caveats⟨56⟩\n  * Source & license⟨57⟩\n\n\n#   ⟨58⟩ D05 Annotated — the full MMAD chain-of-thought corpus \nThe complete reasoning-augmented version of `AI4Manufacturing/D05`⟨59⟩ (MMAD, multimodal industrial anomaly-detection MCQ): **34,414 records** , every one with a teacher-written **chain-of-thought** ending in `FINAL ANSWER`. This is the **merge of two tracks** that were built (and are also released) separately, because they make different claims about the answer:  \n| Track  | Records  | Answer (`annot`)  | Also released as  |  \n| --- | --- | --- | --- |  \n| **Track 1 — rationalized**  | 31,405  | the **original MMAD gold** (reliable, source-derived) — unchanged for all but 19 adjudicated records (see fix package below; 4 of those use `answer: null`)  | `D05-1-annotated`⟨60⟩  |  \n| **Track 2a — re-solved**  | 3,009  |  **teacher-corrected** : the teacher independently re-identified the defect and could reject the MMAD label (605 changed, 75 reject all options → `answer: null`)  | `D05-2a-annotated`⟨61⟩  |  \nTrack 1 covers the question types whose MMAD golds are reliable (Anomaly Detection, Defect Localization / Description, Object Classification / Analysis / Structure / Details, and Defect Classification on DS-MVTec). Track 2a covers Defect Classification on the _label-poor_ sources (VisA, PKU-GoodsAD, MVTec-LOCO), where MMAD's answers were model-assigned and frequently wrong. The under-determined \"Defect Analysis\" type is excluded, as are 474 Track-2a records that failed the correctness gate.\n**Filter by track** with `metadata.cot.source`: `\"D05_track1_rationalized\"` vs `\"D05_track2a_resolve\"`.\n##   ⟨52⟩ Schema   \n| field  | description  |  \n| --- | --- |  \n| `query`  | the original MMAD multiple-choice question (directive updated to \"Answer with the option content.\" — see fix package below)  |  \n| `image`  | the test image (HF `Image`, unchanged)  |  \n| `annot`  |  `{answer, answer_text, question_type}` — original gold (Track 1) or corrected (Track 2a; see above)  |  \n| `reasoning`  | teacher chain-of-thought, grounded only in the test image, ending `FINAL ANSWER: …`  |  \n|  `cate` / `task`  | unchanged from the base dataset  |  \n| `metadata`  | original MMAD metadata + a `cot` provenance block: annotator model, method (`rationalized` / `rationalized_regenerated` / `re_solved_gold_corrected`), the faithfulness screen/gate verdict, any regeneration record, and for Track 2a the original MMAD gold  |  \n##   ⟨53⟩ Roles \n**Roles:** `reasoning` is the SFT imitation target — its `FINAL ANSWER` segment is the model-facing answer format; `annot` is the machine-parseable gold used for verification and reward parsing, **not** an output-format target.\n##   ⟨54⟩ How it was built \n  * **Track 1 (gold-conditioned, improve-never-drop):** gpt-5-mini wrote reasoning justifying the reliable gold, grounded teacher-side by a defect-free reference image (+ segmentation mask for defect subtypes) that is **never leaked** into the text. Every CoT was screened for faithfulness (Claude Sonnet 5); flagged over-reads were **regenerated** with the critique fed back and replaced only when clearly better. Nothing dropped; ~87% of CoTs score faithfulness ≥ 3, the residual is documented per-record.\n  * **Track 2a (re-solved):** Claude Opus 4.8 independently determined the defect (free to reject the proposed label); an independent judge gated answer correctness; failures were dropped.\n  * Both tracks are leak-audited (no references to the reference image / mask / provided answer).\n\n\n##   ⟨55⟩ 2026-07-18 fix package \nThe data files were revised in place. This merged corpus inherits the fix packages of both tracks — **29 corrected records in total** (19 Track-1 + 10 Track-2a) and **79 null-answer records** (4 Track-1 + 75 Track-2a):\n  * **Query directive (both tracks).** The MCQ instruction now reads **\"Answer with the option content.\"** — previously it asked for the option letter, contradicting the answer format actually used by `reasoning` / `FINAL ANSWER`.\n  * **FINAL canonicalization.** All 3,009 Track-2a `reasoning` fields now end with a canonical `FINAL ANSWER: <answer_text>` line.\n  * **Track-1 MMAD-gold adjudication: 19 records'`annot` corrected.** An adjudication pass (unconditioned **claude-opus-4-8 re-solve** + independent **claude-sonnet-4-6 gate**) overturned the original MMAD gold on all 19; corrections were **operator-verified visually on all distinct case types**. Each carries `metadata.cot.original_mmad_gold` plus the full adjudication verdict. **10 of the 19 are a systematic mirrored-gold defect in VisA`pcb4`** (micro-USB position golds on the wrong side) — an upstream MMAD/VisA issue. **4 of the 19** use the null convention (`answer: null` — no offered option is true).\n  * **Track-2a answer-matcher bug.** **10 records'`annot` corrected** for a fuzzy answer-matcher bug (fix + hard assert now in the pipeline); per-record provenance in `metadata.cot.annot_correction` with `original_annot`.\n  * **Gate visibility (Track 2a).** **249 records carry`metadata.cot.gate.keep = false`** — retained under improve-never-drop. Filter recipe for strict training: drop rows where `gate.keep` is `false`.\n\n\nCounts verified by the corpus contradiction re-scan (0 contradictions, 2026-07-18).\n##   ⟨56⟩ Intended use & caveats \n  * For **non-commercial research** on manufacturing-domain vision-language reasoning (CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0, inherited from MMAD).\n  * `reasoning` is **teacher-generated and model-gated** , not human-verified. Track-2a answers are model-corrected; the original MMAD gold is always retained in `metadata.cot.original_mmad_gold`. Track-1 answers are the original MMAD golds, except for the 19 adjudicated records disclosed in the fix package above (each retains `metadata.cot.original_mmad_gold`).\n  * The two track repos remain available for consumers who want only one claim type.\n\n\n##   ⟨57⟩ Source & license \nDerived from MMAD (via `AI4Manufacturing/D05`), which aggregates MVTec-AD, MVTec-LOCO, VisA, and PKU-GoodsAD. Licensed **CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0**. Please cite MMAD and the underlying source datasets.\nCopy to bucket new \n\nDownloads last month\n    47\nTotal file size: 16.3 GB\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨62⟩ Privacy⟨63⟩ About⟨64⟩ Careers⟨65⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\n",
